pair_id,registered_endpoint,published_endpoint,similarity_score,ssi,routing,llm_model,llm_switch_type,llm_reasoning,llm_confidence,llm_comparability,llm_flag,llm_disclosed_exploratory,llm_results_driven,llm_switch_forms,llm_confidence_score,llm_classification_label,llm_primary_endpoint_match,llm_published_primary_extracted,llm_actual_change_evidence,llm_missing_detail_only,llm_adjudication_guardrail,llm_endpoint_comparisons,human_reviewed,human_decision,human_final_class,human_poolable,override_reason,reviewer_initials,review_timestamp,pipeline_version,created_at
NCT00493649_24007746,Disease-free Survival (DFS) Rate at 2 Years in TOP2A-amplified and in TOP2A-nonamplified HER2+ ESBC Patients Treated With TC+H. [Time Frame: 2 years],"493 patients were enrolled between June 15, 2007, and Aug 5, 2009. After a median follow-up of 36·1 months (IQR 35·5-36·7), 2-year DFS was 97·8% (95% CI 94·2-99·2) and 2-year overall survival was 99·5% (95% CI 96·2-99·9) for the 190 patients with TOP2A-amplified disease; 2-year DFS was 97·9% (95% CI 94·9-99·1) and 2-year overall survival was 98·8% (95% CI 96·2-99·6) for the 248 patients with TOP2A-non-amplified disease; 55 patients were not assessable for TOP2A status. In the 486 patients who received at least one dose of study drug, the most common adverse events of any grade were fatigue (284 patients, 58·4%), neutropenia (250, 51·4%), and nausea (217, 44·7%). The most common grade 3-4 toxic effects were neutropenia (229, 47·1%), febrile neutropenia (30, 6·2%), fatigue (21, 4·3%), and diarrhoea (16, 3·3%). Cardiac dysfunction occurred in 29 (6·0%) patients (12 [2·5%] grade 1, 15 [3·1%] grade 2, and two [0·4%] grade 3). 23 patients had at least one study-related serious adverse event. 16 patients stopped trastuzumab because of cardiac dysfunction.",0.6983,30.17,llm,gpt-5.6-luna,concordant,"The published primary outcome is the same 2-year DFS endpoint registered for TOP2A-defined patient groups. The publication also reports 2-year overall survival, which was a registered secondary outcome, and does not replace or demote the registered DFS endpoint. The cMyc-stratified secondary outcomes are not reported in the provided publication text, but missing secondary outcomes do not constitute primary outcome switching. The original prospective registry version and any amendment history are unavailable. The current registry entry was used cautiously; its wording alone does not support classification as an outcome switch. The current registered primary is directly reported in the publication.",high,True,False,False,False,,0.98,Concordant (no change),clinically equivalent,2-year disease-free survival (DFS) in patients with TOP2A-amplified and TOP2A-non-amplified disease,,True,,"[{""registered_endpoint"": ""Disease-free Survival (DFS) Rate at 2 Years in TOP2A-amplified and TOP2A-nonamplified HER2+ ESBC Patients Treated With TC+H"", ""published_corresponding_endpoint"": ""2-year DFS reported separately for TOP2A-amplified and TOP2A-non-amplified disease"", ""same_construct"": true, ""same_timeframe"": true, ""same_definition"": true, ""same_population"": true, ""same_measurement_method"": null, ""registered_endpoint_reported"": true, ""additional_endpoint_present"": false, ""additional_endpoint_disclosed"": false, ""change_disclosed"": null, ""actual_change_evidence"": [], ""classification_label"": ""Concordant (no change)""}]",auto_accepted,confirm,concordant,True,,AUTO,,pipeline_v4.5,2026-09-05T20:46:36.478875+00:00
NCT01816594_28923573,Pathological Complete Response (pCR) Rate at the Time of Surgery - All Participants [Time Frame: After 6 weeks] | Pathological Complete Response (pCR) Rate at the Time of Surgery - PIK3CA Wild Type (WT) [Time Frame: After 6 weeks] | Pathological Complete Response (pCR) Rate at the Time of Surgery - PIK3CA Mutant (MT) [Time Frame: After 6 weeks],"Recruitment was suspended mainly due to liver toxicity after enrolment of 50 of the planned 256 patients. In each arm (buparlisib n = 25; placebo n = 25) 21 patients (84%) had wild type PIK3CA and 4 patients (16%) had mutant PIK3CA. Overall, pCR rate was similar between buparlisib and placebo arms (32.0% versus 40%; one-sided P = 0.811). A trend towards higher ORR (68.8% versus 33.3%; P = 0.053) and a significant decrease in Ki67 (75% versus 26.7%; P = 0.021) was observed in buparlisib versus placebo arm in the ER+ subgroup (Pinteraction = 0.03).",0.6298,37.02,llm,gpt-5.6-luna,concordant,"The registered and published primary clinical construct is pCR. The publication explicitly reports overall pCR, which corresponds to the all-participant registered primary endpoint. The absence of separately stated PIK3CA-stratified pCR results in the supplied text does not demonstrate replacement or demotion of the registered primary endpoint. ORR and Ki67 are additional reported analyses/outcomes, but their presence does not constitute outcome switching. Registry history was unavailable, so the current entry cannot be confirmed as the original prospective registration. The current registered primary endpoints are all pCR endpoints, including overall pCR and PIK3CA-stratified pCR. Because the publication reports overall pCR as the primary result and there is no evidence that a different endpoint replaced it, no switch is assigned based on the later registry wording.",high,True,True,False,False,,0.86,Concordant (no change),clinically equivalent,Overall pCR rate at surgery: 32.0% with buparlisib versus 40% with placebo.,,True,,"[{""registered_endpoint"": ""pCR rate at the time of surgery after 6 weeks — all participants"", ""published_corresponding_endpoint"": ""Overall pCR rate: 32.0% versus 40% between treatment arms"", ""same_construct"": true, ""same_timeframe"": null, ""same_definition"": true, ""same_population"": true, ""same_measurement_method"": null, ""registered_endpoint_reported"": true, ""additional_endpoint_present"": false, ""additional_endpoint_disclosed"": false, ""change_disclosed"": null, ""actual_change_evidence"": [], ""classification_label"": ""Concordant (no change)""}, {""registered_endpoint"": ""pCR rate at the time of surgery after 6 weeks — PIK3CA wild type"", ""published_corresponding_endpoint"": ""No separate PIK3CA wild-type pCR rate is stated in the supplied publication text; only overall pCR is reported."", ""same_construct"": true, ""same_timeframe"": null, ""same_definition"": null, ""same_population"": null, ""same_measurement_method"": null, ""registered_endpoint_reported"": false, ""additional_endpoint_present"": false, ""additional_endpoint_disclosed"": false, ""change_disclosed"": null, ""actual_change_evidence"": [], ""classification_label"": ""Concordant (no change)""}, {""registered_endpoint"": ""pCR rate at the time of surgery after 6 weeks — PIK3CA mutant"", ""published_corresponding_endpoint"": ""No separate PIK3CA-mutant pCR rate is stated in the supplied publication text; only overall pCR is reported."", ""same_construct"": true, ""same_timeframe"": null, ""same_definition"": null, ""same_population"": null, ""same_measurement_method"": null, ""registered_endpoint_reported"": false, ""additional_endpoint_present"": false, ""additional_endpoint_disclosed"": false, ""change_disclosed"": null, ""actual_change_evidence"": [], ""classification_label"": ""Concordant (no change)""}]",auto_accepted,confirm,concordant,True,,AUTO,,pipeline_v4.5,2026-09-05T20:46:57.371871+00:00
NCT01160211_32822287,"Progression Free Survival (PFS) Events in Lapatinib + Trastuzumab + Aromatase Inhibitor (AI) vs. Trastuzumab + Aromatase Inhibitor (AI) [Time Frame: From date of randomization until date of progression or date of death from any cause, whichever comes first, assessed up approximately 5 years] | Median Kaplan Meier Estimates for PFS in Lapatinib + Trastuzumab + Aromatase Inhibitor (AI) vs. Trastuzumab + Aromatase Inhibitor (AI) [Time Frame: From date of randomization until date of progression or date of death from any cause, whichever comes first, assessed up approximately 5 years]","primary end point; superior PFS was observed with LAP plus TRAS plus AI versus TRAS plus AI (median PFS, 11 v 5",0.7048,29.52,llm,gpt-5.6-luna,concordant,"The registered and published primary outcomes are both PFS for the same principal treatment comparison. Reporting median PFS and a hazard ratio represents analysis and presentation of the registered PFS endpoint, not a different endpoint. The publication does not explicitly report a different timeframe, definition, population, or measurement method. The absence of the full registered timeframe from the extracted publication text is missing detail only, not evidence of modification. Several registered secondary outcomes are not reported in the provided text, but their omission does not constitute primary outcome switching. No registry change history is available, so the original prospective primary outcome cannot be independently confirmed. The current registry entry is therefore treated cautiously. Its PFS wording is clinically concordant with the published primary PFS outcome, and no major switch is inferred from the current wording alone.",high,True,False,False,False,,0.97,Concordant (no change),clinically equivalent,"Progression-free survival (PFS), with superior PFS for lapatinib + trastuzumab + aromatase inhibitor versus trastuzumab + aromatase inhibitor; median PFS 11 versus 5.6 months.",,True,,"[{""registered_endpoint"": ""PFS events in lapatinib + trastuzumab + AI versus trastuzumab + AI, from randomization until progression or death, assessed up to approximately 5 years."", ""published_corresponding_endpoint"": ""PFS comparing lapatinib + trastuzumab + AI versus trastuzumab + AI, reported as median PFS and hazard ratio."", ""same_construct"": true, ""same_timeframe"": null, ""same_definition"": true, ""same_population"": true, ""same_measurement_method"": null, ""registered_endpoint_reported"": true, ""additional_endpoint_present"": false, ""additional_endpoint_disclosed"": false, ""change_disclosed"": null, ""actual_change_evidence"": [], ""classification_label"": ""Concordant (no change)""}, {""registered_endpoint"": ""Median Kaplan-Meier estimates for PFS in lapatinib + trastuzumab + AI versus trastuzumab + AI, from randomization until progression or death, assessed up to approximately 5 years."", ""published_corresponding_endpoint"": ""Median PFS comparing lapatinib + trastuzumab + AI versus trastuzumab + AI."", ""same_construct"": true, ""same_timeframe"": null, ""same_definition"": true, ""same_population"": true, ""same_measurement_method"": true, ""registered_endpoint_reported"": true, ""additional_endpoint_present"": false, ""additional_endpoint_disclosed"": false, ""change_disclosed"": null, ""actual_change_evidence"": [], ""classification_label"": ""Concordant (no change)""}]",auto_accepted,confirm,concordant,True,,AUTO,,pipeline_v4.5,2026-09-05T20:47:10.681981+00:00
NCT02040857_31250880,"2-Year Treatment Discontinuation Rate [Time Frame: Evaluate upon completion of palbociclib, up to 2 years of treatment completion.]","Overall, 162 patients initiated palbociclib; over half had stage III disease (52%) and most received prior chemotherapy (80%). A total of 102 patients (63%) completed 2 years of palbociclib; 50 patients discontinued early for protocol-related reasons (31%, 95% CI 24% to 39%, P = 0.001), and 10 discontinued due to protocol-unrelated reasons. The cumulative incidence of protocol-related discontinuation was 21% (95% CI 14% to 27%) at 12 months from start of treatment. Rates of palbociclib-related toxicity were congruent with the metastatic experience, and there were no cases of febrile neutropenia. Ninety-one patients (56%) required at least one dose reduction.",0.7594,24.06,llm,gpt-5.6-luna,concordant,"The publication reports the same clinical construct as the registered primary endpoint: discontinuation or completion of 2 years of palbociclib. Reporting a 12-month cumulative incidence as an additional analysis does not replace the 2-year endpoint. The registry does not specify a sufficiently detailed discontinuation definition to establish a definition change, and absent registry history prevents comparison with an earlier version. Only the current registry entry was available, and the original prospective version and any amendments could not be established. The current primary outcome was therefore used cautiously; no major switch is assigned on the basis of the current wording alone.",high,True,False,False,False,,0.9,Concordant (no change),clinically equivalent,"Treatment discontinuation/completion of 2 years of palbociclib, including protocol-related discontinuation assessed through 2 years.",,True,,"[{""registered_endpoint"": ""2-Year Treatment Discontinuation Rate"", ""published_corresponding_endpoint"": ""Treatment discontinuation and completion of 2 years of palbociclib; protocol-related discontinuation was reported, with cumulative incidence also reported at 12 months."", ""same_construct"": true, ""same_timeframe"": true, ""same_definition"": null, ""same_population"": true, ""same_measurement_method"": null, ""registered_endpoint_reported"": true, ""additional_endpoint_present"": false, ""additional_endpoint_disclosed"": false, ""change_disclosed"": null, ""actual_change_evidence"": [], ""classification_label"": ""Concordant (no change)""}]",auto_accepted,confirm,concordant,True,,AUTO,,pipeline_v4.5,2026-09-05T20:47:23.325501+00:00
NCT00811135_22467666,"Percentage of Participants With a Best Overall Response (BOR) of Confirmed Complete Response (CR) or Partial Response (PR) [Time Frame: Screening until disease progression (assessed at screening, every 6 weeks up to Week 36, thereafter every 9 weeks during treatment period, and then every 3 months during follow-up, up to approximately 4 years)]","primary endpoint, was 73% (95% confidence interval [CI], 62%-82%), comprising 7% complete and 66% partial responses",0.6211,37.89,llm,gpt-5.6-luna,concordant,"The published overall response rate can be directly reconstructed from complete and partial responses and represents the same response endpoint as the registered BOR of confirmed CR or PR. The publication does not restate all registry qualifiers, but their absence from the provided text is not affirmative evidence of a changed definition, timeframe, population, or assessment method. No registry change history was available and the original prospective outcome could not be verified. The current registry primary outcome was used cautiously; the later wording alone is insufficient to assign a major switch.",high,True,False,False,False,,0.94,Concordant (no change),clinically equivalent,"Overall response rate of 73% (95% CI, 62%-82%), comprising 7% complete responses and 66% partial responses",,True,,"[{""registered_endpoint"": ""Best overall response of confirmed complete response or partial response"", ""published_corresponding_endpoint"": ""Overall response rate comprising complete and partial responses"", ""same_construct"": true, ""same_timeframe"": null, ""same_definition"": null, ""same_population"": null, ""same_measurement_method"": null, ""registered_endpoint_reported"": true, ""additional_endpoint_present"": false, ""additional_endpoint_disclosed"": false, ""change_disclosed"": null, ""actual_change_evidence"": [], ""classification_label"": ""Concordant (no change)""}]",auto_accepted,confirm,concordant,True,,AUTO,,pipeline_v4.5,2026-09-05T20:47:32.245405+00:00
NCT03250676_40830892,"Phase 1: Number of Participants With Dose-limiting Toxicities (DLTs) [Time Frame: Cycle 1 (Cycle length=28 days)] | Phase 1 and Phase 2: Objective Response Rate (ORR) [Time Frame: Phase 1 and Phase 2: From the first dose of study drug to the first date of documentation of progressive disease (PD) or death, whichever occurred first (up to 33 months)] | Phase 1 and Phase 2: Duration of Response (DoR) [Time Frame: Phase 1 and Phase 2: From the first dose of study drug to the first date of documentation of PD or death, whichever occurred first (up to 33 months)] | Phase 1 and Phase 2: Disease Control Rate (DCR) [Time Frame: Phase 1 and Phase 2: From the first dose of study drug to the first date of documentation of PD or death, whichever occurred first (up to 33 months)] | Phase 1 and Phase 2: Clinical Benefit Rate (CBR) [Time Frame: Phase 1 and Phase 2: From the first dose of study drug to the first date of documentation of PD or death, whichever occurred first (up to 33 months)] | Phase 1 and Phase 2: Progression-free Survival (PFS) [Time Frame: Phase 1 and Phase 2: From the first dose of study drug to the first date of documentation of PD or death, whichever occurred first (up to 33 months)] | Phase 1 and Phase 2: Overall Survival (OS) [Time Frame: Phase 1 and Phase 2: From the first dose of study drug to date of death or last known alive (up to 63 months)]","primary endpoints were RP2D determination (phase 1) and objective response rate (ORR) (phase 2, investigator-assessed per RECIST v1",0.7298,27.02,llm,gpt-5.6-luna,major_switch,"The Phase 2 published primary endpoint, ORR, is clinically equivalent to the current registered ORR. However, the Phase 1 published primary endpoint is RP2D determination, whereas the current registry identifies the Phase 1 primary endpoint as the number of participants with DLTs; these are related but distinct constructs. Because the original registry version is unavailable and the publication text provides no explicit protocol-amendment explanation, the discrepancy supports a moderate/partly disclosed classification rather than a major undisclosed switch. Registry change history is unavailable. The current registry entry was used cautiously, but it cannot establish the original prospective primary endpoint. Therefore, the Phase 1 discrepancy is not classified as a major undisclosed switch solely on the basis of the current registry wording. Guardrail applied: Endpoint 3: clinical-construct equivalence was not established. Endpoint 4: clinical-construct equivalence was not established. Endpoint 5: clinical-construct equivalence was not established. Endpoint 6: clinical-construct equivalence was not established. Endpoint 7: clinical-construct equivalence was not established.",medium,False,True,False,True,primary_replaced | prespecified_omitted,0.65,Outcome switch — major / undisclosed,different,RP2D determination in Phase 1 and investigator-assessed Objective Response Rate (ORR) in Phase 2 per RECIST v1.,"The current registry identifies the Phase 1 primary outcome as the number of participants with DLTs, whereas the publication identifies RP2D determination as the Phase 1 primary endpoint.",False,Endpoint 3: clinical-construct equivalence was not established. Endpoint 4: clinical-construct equivalence was not established. Endpoint 5: clinical-construct equivalence was not established. Endpoint 6: clinical-construct equivalence was not established. Endpoint 7: clinical-construct equivalence was not established.,"[{""registered_endpoint"": ""Phase 1: Number of Participants With Dose-limiting Toxicities (DLTs) during Cycle 1."", ""published_corresponding_endpoint"": ""RP2D determination in Phase 1."", ""same_construct"": false, ""same_timeframe"": null, ""same_definition"": null, ""same_population"": null, ""same_measurement_method"": null, ""registered_endpoint_reported"": false, ""additional_endpoint_present"": false, ""additional_endpoint_disclosed"": false, ""change_disclosed"": false, ""actual_change_evidence"": [""The current registry identifies the Phase 1 primary outcome as the number of participants with DLTs, whereas the publication identifies RP2D determination as the Phase 1 primary endpoint.""], ""classification_label"": ""Outcome switch — major / undisclosed""}, {""registered_endpoint"": ""Phase 1 and Phase 2: Objective Response Rate (ORR), from first dose until documentation of progressive disease or death, up to 33 months."", ""published_corresponding_endpoint"": ""Phase 2 investigator-assessed Objective Response Rate (ORR) per RECIST v1."", ""same_construct"": true, ""same_timeframe"": null, ""same_definition"": null, ""same_population"": null, ""same_measurement_method"": null, ""registered_endpoint_reported"": true, ""additional_endpoint_present"": false, ""additional_endpoint_disclosed"": false, ""change_disclosed"": null, ""actual_change_evidence"": [], ""classification_label"": ""Concordant (no change)""}, {""registered_endpoint"": ""Phase 1 and Phase 2: Duration of Response (DoR), from first dose until progressive disease or death, up to 33 months."", ""published_corresponding_endpoint"": ""Not identified in the provided publication text."", ""same_construct"": null, ""same_timeframe"": null, ""same_definition"": null, ""same_population"": null, ""same_measurement_method"": null, ""registered_endpoint_reported"": false, ""additional_endpoint_present"": false, ""additional_endpoint_disclosed"": false, ""change_disclosed"": null, ""actual_change_evidence"": [], ""classification_label"": ""Concordant (no change)""}, {""registered_endpoint"": ""Phase 1 and Phase 2: Disease Control Rate (DCR), from first dose until progressive disease or death, up to 33 months."", ""published_corresponding_endpoint"": ""Not identified in the provided publication text."", ""same_construct"": null, ""same_timeframe"": null, ""same_definition"": null, ""same_population"": null, ""same_measurement_method"": null, ""registered_endpoint_reported"": false, ""additional_endpoint_present"": false, ""additional_endpoint_disclosed"": false, ""change_disclosed"": null, ""actual_change_evidence"": [], ""classification_label"": ""Concordant (no change)""}, {""registered_endpoint"": ""Phase 1 and Phase 2: Clinical Benefit Rate (CBR), from first dose until progressive disease or death, up to 33 months."", ""published_corresponding_endpoint"": ""Not identified in the provided publication text."", ""same_construct"": null, ""same_timeframe"": null, ""same_definition"": null, ""same_population"": null, ""same_measurement_method"": null, ""registered_endpoint_reported"": false, ""additional_endpoint_present"": false, ""additional_endpoint_disclosed"": false, ""change_disclosed"": null, ""actual_change_evidence"": [], ""classification_label"": ""Concordant (no change)""}, {""registered_endpoint"": ""Phase 1 and Phase 2: Progression-free Survival (PFS), from first dose until progressive disease or death, up to 33 months."", ""published_corresponding_endpoint"": ""Not identified in the provided publication text."", ""same_construct"": null, ""same_timeframe"": null, ""same_definition"": null, ""same_population"": null, ""same_measurement_method"": null, ""registered_endpoint_reported"": false, ""additional_endpoint_present"": false, ""additional_endpoint_disclosed"": false, ""change_disclosed"": null, ""actual_change_evidence"": [], ""classification_label"": ""Concordant (no change)""}, {""registered_endpoint"": ""Phase 1 and Phase 2: Overall Survival (OS), from first dose until death or last known alive, up to 63 months."", ""published_corresponding_endpoint"": ""Not identified in the provided publication text."", ""same_construct"": null, ""same_timeframe"": null, ""same_definition"": null, ""same_population"": null, ""same_measurement_method"": null, ""registered_endpoint_reported"": false, ""additional_endpoint_present"": false, ""additional_endpoint_disclosed"": false, ""change_disclosed"": null, ""actual_change_evidence"": [], ""classification_label"": ""Concordant (no change)""}]",auto_accepted,confirm,major_switch,False,,AUTO,,pipeline_v4.5,2026-09-05T20:47:54.504228+00:00
NCT01853748_34077270,"Number of Participants of Clinically Relevant Toxicities (CRT) [Time Frame: 5 years after completion of study treatment or until death, whichever occurs first.] | 3-year Disease Free Survival (DFS) Rate of Trastuzumab Emtansine (TDM-1) [Time Frame: 3 years]","The analysis population includes all 497 patients who initiated protocol therapy (383 T-DM1 and 114 TH). CRTs were experienced by 46% of patients on T-DM1 and 47% of patients on TH (P = .83). The 3-year iDFS for T-DM1 was 97.8% (95% CI, 96.3 to 99.3), which rejected the null hypothesis (P < .0001). Serially collected patient-reported outcomes indicated that patients treated with T-DM1 had less neuropathy and alopecia and better work productivity compared with patients on TH.",0.5917,40.83,llm,gpt-5.6-luna,concordant,"The publication reports both registered primary constructs: CRTs and 3-year disease-free survival. The use of iDFS rather than DFS is clinically compatible in this context, and no affirmative evidence demonstrates a different timeframe, definition, population, or measurement method. The publication's omission of some registry qualifiers and secondary outcomes does not establish primary outcome switching. No registry change history is available and the original prospective version cannot be confirmed. The current registry entry was therefore used cautiously; its later wording alone is insufficient evidence of switching. Both current registered primary outcomes are reported in the publication.",high,True,True,False,False,,0.9,Concordant (no change),clinically equivalent,Clinically relevant toxicities (CRTs) and 3-year invasive disease-free survival (iDFS) for T-DM1,,True,,"[{""registered_endpoint"": ""Number of Participants of Clinically Relevant Toxicities (CRT)"", ""published_corresponding_endpoint"": ""Proportion of patients experiencing clinically relevant toxicities (CRTs)"", ""same_construct"": true, ""same_timeframe"": null, ""same_definition"": true, ""same_population"": null, ""same_measurement_method"": null, ""registered_endpoint_reported"": true, ""additional_endpoint_present"": false, ""additional_endpoint_disclosed"": false, ""change_disclosed"": null, ""actual_change_evidence"": [], ""classification_label"": ""Concordant (no change)""}, {""registered_endpoint"": ""3-year Disease Free Survival (DFS) Rate of Trastuzumab Emtansine (T-DM1)"", ""published_corresponding_endpoint"": ""3-year invasive disease-free survival (iDFS) for T-DM1"", ""same_construct"": true, ""same_timeframe"": true, ""same_definition"": null, ""same_population"": null, ""same_measurement_method"": null, ""registered_endpoint_reported"": true, ""additional_endpoint_present"": false, ""additional_endpoint_disclosed"": false, ""change_disclosed"": null, ""actual_change_evidence"": [], ""classification_label"": ""Concordant (no change)""}]",auto_accepted,confirm,concordant,True,,AUTO,,pipeline_v4.5,2026-09-05T20:48:10.864762+00:00
NCT03371017_38755096,Overall Survival (OS) in PD-L1-positive Population [Time Frame: Time from randomization to death (Up to 68 months)] | OS in Modified Intent-to-treat (mITT) Population [Time Frame: Time from randomization to death (Up to 68 months)],"Among 354 patients with rapidly relapsing PD-L1-positive aTNBC, 68% had a disease-free interval of <6 months and 73% received carboplatin/gemcitabine. The OS hazard ratio was 0.93 (95% confidence interval 0.73-1.20, P = 0.59; median 11.2 months with placebo versus 12.1 months with atezolizumab). mITT and subgroup results were consistent. Median PFS was 4 months across treatment arms and populations. ORRs were 28% with placebo versus 40% with atezolizumab. Adverse events (predominantly haematological) were similar between arms and as expected with atezolizumab plus carboplatin/gemcitabine or capecitabine following recent chemotherapy exposure.",0.6018,39.82,llm,gpt-5.6-luna,concordant,"The registered and published primary endpoints are the same clinical construct: overall survival measured as time to death. The publication reports OS in the PD-L1-positive population and addresses the mITT population. The absence of the registered maximum follow-up wording from the provided publication text is only missing detail and is not evidence of a changed timeframe. PFS and ORR are reported as secondary outcomes and do not replace OS. No registry change history or original prospective version was available, so the current registry entry was used cautiously. The current registered primary endpoints are OS in the PD-L1-positive and mITT populations, and the publication reports OS in these populations. The absence of the original version prevents confirmation of the earliest prospective wording but does not support a switch.",high,True,False,False,False,,0.96,Concordant (no change),clinically equivalent,"Overall survival (OS), reported with an OS hazard ratio and median OS; results were reported for the PD-L1-positive population, with mITT and subgroup results described as consistent.",,True,,"[{""registered_endpoint"": ""OS in the PD-L1-positive population: time from randomization to death, up to 68 months."", ""published_corresponding_endpoint"": ""OS in patients with rapidly relapsing PD-L1-positive aTNBC, reported using an OS hazard ratio and median OS."", ""same_construct"": true, ""same_timeframe"": null, ""same_definition"": true, ""same_population"": true, ""same_measurement_method"": null, ""registered_endpoint_reported"": true, ""additional_endpoint_present"": false, ""additional_endpoint_disclosed"": false, ""change_disclosed"": null, ""actual_change_evidence"": [], ""classification_label"": ""Concordant (no change)""}, {""registered_endpoint"": ""OS in the mITT population: time from randomization to death, up to 68 months."", ""published_corresponding_endpoint"": ""OS in the mITT population; the publication states that mITT results were consistent."", ""same_construct"": true, ""same_timeframe"": null, ""same_definition"": true, ""same_population"": true, ""same_measurement_method"": null, ""registered_endpoint_reported"": true, ""additional_endpoint_present"": false, ""additional_endpoint_disclosed"": false, ""change_disclosed"": null, ""actual_change_evidence"": [], ""classification_label"": ""Concordant (no change)""}]",auto_accepted,confirm,concordant,True,,AUTO,,pipeline_v4.5,2026-09-05T20:48:26.038428+00:00
NCT01926886_32240454,Percentage of Participants With Adverse Events (AEs) and Serious Adverse Events (SAEs) [Time Frame: Up to 45 months],"Between November 2013 and December 2014, 23 centres enrolled 102 patients in the intent-to-treat population of which 101 patients entered the safety population. No new safety signals were detected with as expected, more mild administration site events with trastuzumab SC when compared to IV treatment. All patients agreed that they had benefit from at home administration to a large (18/81; 22%) or very large (63/81; 78%) extent. All HCPs (21/21) agreed that SC is the quickest method from start of preparation to finish of administration and that less resource use is needed.",0.4066,59.34,llm,gpt-5.6-luna,concordant,"The registered primary endpoint is safety based on AEs and SAEs. The publication reports safety findings as its leading clinical outcome, including no new safety signals and administration-site events. Patient and HCP satisfaction or home-administration assessments are additional outcomes, largely corresponding to registered secondary outcomes, and do not replace the safety endpoint. Exact timeframe, AE/SAE definition, and measurement details are not fully stated in the supplied publication text, but their absence is not evidence of modification. No registry change history is available, and the original prospective primary outcome cannot be verified. The current registry entry was therefore used cautiously; the current primary safety outcome should not be treated as definitively original, but there is no basis for assigning a major switch from the available information.",high,True,False,False,False,,0.9,Concordant (no change),clinically equivalent,"Safety, assessed by adverse events and serious adverse events; the publication reports no new safety signals and more mild administration-site events with trastuzumab SC compared with IV treatment.",,True,,"[{""registered_endpoint"": ""Percentage of Participants With Adverse Events (AEs) and Serious Adverse Events (SAEs) [Time Frame: Up to 45 months]"", ""published_corresponding_endpoint"": ""Safety assessed through reported adverse events and serious adverse events; no new safety signals were detected, with more mild administration-site events reported for trastuzumab SC versus IV treatment."", ""same_construct"": true, ""same_timeframe"": null, ""same_definition"": null, ""same_population"": true, ""same_measurement_method"": null, ""registered_endpoint_reported"": true, ""additional_endpoint_present"": false, ""additional_endpoint_disclosed"": false, ""change_disclosed"": null, ""actual_change_evidence"": [], ""classification_label"": ""Concordant (no change)""}]",auto_accepted,confirm,concordant,True,,AUTO,,pipeline_v4.5,2026-09-05T20:48:39.273521+00:00
NCT01605396_28681171,1. Progression-free Survival (PFS) According to Response Criteria in Solid Tumors Version 1.1 (RECIST 1.1) Based on Blinded Independent Central Review (BICR) [Time Frame: From Day 1 through last post-study efficacy follow-up (up to ~19 months)],Median PFS was 23.3 weeks for R/D/E versus 31.9 weeks for R/E (hazard ratio 1.18; 80% CI 0.81-1.72; P = 0.565). Grade 3-5 adverse events were reported in 67.5% of patients in the R/E arm and 59.0% in the R/D/E arm. Stomatitis (95.0 vs. 76.9%; P = 0.021) and pneumonitis (22.5 vs. 5.1%; P = 0.027) occurred more frequently in the R/E than the R/D/E arm; hyperglycemia (27.5 vs. 28.2%) occurred at a similar rate.,0.4826,51.74,llm,gpt-5.6-luna,concordant,"The registered and published primary outcomes are both progression-free survival. Reporting median PFS and a hazard ratio does not change the endpoint. The publication does not affirmatively report a different timeframe, definition, population, or measurement method; the absence of repeated RECIST/BICR qualifiers is missing detail only. The unreported registered secondary outcomes do not constitute primary outcome switching. The original prospective registry version and any amendment history are unavailable. The current registry entry was therefore used cautiously; no major switch is inferred from the later wording alone.",high,True,True,False,False,,0.92,Concordant (no change),clinically equivalent,"Median progression-free survival (PFS), reported for R/D/E versus R/E",,True,,"[{""registered_endpoint"": ""Progression-free Survival (PFS) according to RECIST 1.1 based on BICR"", ""published_corresponding_endpoint"": ""Median progression-free survival (PFS)"", ""same_construct"": true, ""same_timeframe"": null, ""same_definition"": null, ""same_population"": null, ""same_measurement_method"": null, ""registered_endpoint_reported"": true, ""additional_endpoint_present"": false, ""additional_endpoint_disclosed"": false, ""change_disclosed"": null, ""actual_change_evidence"": [], ""classification_label"": ""Concordant (no change)""}]",auto_accepted,confirm,concordant,True,,AUTO,,pipeline_v4.5,2026-09-05T20:48:48.905457+00:00
NCT01125566_26822398,"Progression-free Survival (PFS) [Time Frame: From randomization (07Sep2010) until disease progression, death or data cut-off (08Jun2013); Up to 34 months]","Between Aug 26, 2010, and April 26, 2013, we enrolled 508 patients: 339 assigned to the afatinib group and 169 assigned to the trastuzumab group. Recruitment was stopped on April 26, 2013, after a benefit-risk assessment by the independent data monitoring committee was unfavourable for the afatinib group. Patients on afatinib plus vinorelbine had to switch to trastuzumab plus vinorelbine, afatinib monotherapy, vinorelbine monotherapy, or receive treatment outside of the trial. Median follow-up was 9·3 months (IQR 3·7-16·0). Median progression-free survival was 5·5 months (95% CI 5·4-5·6) in the afatinib group and 5·6 months (5·3-7·3) in the trastuzumab group (hazard ratio 1·10 95% CI 0·86-1·41; p=0·43). The most common drug-related adverse events of grade 3 or higher were neutropenia (190 [56%] of 337 patients in the afatinib group vs 102 [60%] of 169 patients in the trastuzumab group), leucopenia (64 [19%] vs 34 [20%]), and diarrhoea (60 [18%] vs none).",0.486,51.4,llm,gpt-5.6-luna,concordant,"The registered primary outcome and published primary outcome are both progression-free survival. The publication reports the registered endpoint directly, although it does not restate every registry timeframe or operational detail. The missing secondary outcomes in the provided extract do not constitute primary outcome switching. No registry change history is available. The current registry entry was therefore used cautiously as the registered comparator; the absence of the original prospective version prevents verification of any earlier wording or amendments. This uncertainty does not support a major switch because the current registered primary and published primary are both PFS.",high,True,False,False,False,,0.97,Concordant (no change),clinically equivalent,"Progression-free survival (PFS), reported as median PFS by treatment group",,True,,"[{""registered_endpoint"": ""Progression-free Survival (PFS)"", ""published_corresponding_endpoint"": ""Progression-free survival (PFS)"", ""same_construct"": true, ""same_timeframe"": null, ""same_definition"": null, ""same_population"": null, ""same_measurement_method"": null, ""registered_endpoint_reported"": true, ""additional_endpoint_present"": false, ""additional_endpoint_disclosed"": false, ""change_disclosed"": null, ""actual_change_evidence"": [], ""classification_label"": ""Concordant (no change)""}]",auto_accepted,confirm,concordant,True,,AUTO,,pipeline_v4.5,2026-09-05T20:48:57.777273+00:00
NCT03633331_38852379,Incidence of Adverse Events [Time Frame: 6 months],"Of the 90 participants (median age 74 years [70-87]) enrolled, 75.6% (95% confidence interval [CI], 65.4-84.0) had grade 3+ AEs by six months. The most frequent grade 3+ AEs were neutropenia (61%), fatigue (4%), and nausea (3%). Febrile neutropenia was uncommon (1.1%). Due to AEs, 36% had dose delays, 34% had dose reductions, 10% had early discontinuations, and 10% had hospitalizations. Compared to those aged 70-74 years, participants aged ≥75 years had higher rates of early discontinuations (5.9% vs 15.9%, a difference of 9.5% [95% CI 3.5%-22.5%]).",0.4826,51.74,llm,gpt-5.6-luna,minor_modification,"The registered and published outcomes address the same clinical construct of adverse-event incidence over six months. However, the publication explicitly uses a grade 3+ severity threshold that is not present in the registered wording, constituting a definition modification. The original registry version and any amendment history are unavailable, so the evidence does not support a moderate or major outcome-switch classification. Registry change history was unavailable. The current registry entry was therefore used cautiously; the original prospective primary outcome cannot be confirmed, and no major switch is assigned solely on the basis of the current wording.",high,False,False,False,False,definition_or_timeframe_changed,0.83,Outcome modification (timeframe/definition/population),modified,Incidence of grade 3+ adverse events by six months,"The registry specifies incidence of adverse events at 6 months without a severity threshold, whereas the publication defines the primary result as grade 3+ adverse events by six months.",False,,"[{""registered_endpoint"": ""Incidence of Adverse Events at 6 months"", ""published_corresponding_endpoint"": ""Incidence of grade 3+ adverse events by 6 months"", ""same_construct"": true, ""same_timeframe"": true, ""same_definition"": false, ""same_population"": null, ""same_measurement_method"": null, ""registered_endpoint_reported"": true, ""additional_endpoint_present"": false, ""additional_endpoint_disclosed"": false, ""change_disclosed"": null, ""actual_change_evidence"": [""The registry specifies incidence of adverse events at 6 months without a severity threshold, whereas the publication defines the primary result as grade 3+ adverse events by six months.""], ""classification_label"": ""Outcome modification (timeframe/definition/population)""}]",auto_accepted,confirm,minor_modification,False,,AUTO,,pipeline_v4.5,2026-09-05T20:49:13.773249+00:00
NCT00066703_24881463,Disease-free Survival [Time Frame: 5-year estimate reported at a median follow-up of 72 months],"After a median follow-up of 68 months, disease-free survival at 5 years was 91.1% in the exemestane-ovarian suppression group and 87.3% in the tamoxifen-ovarian suppression group (hazard ratio for disease recurrence, second invasive cancer, or death, 0.72; 95% confidence interval [CI], 0.60 to 0.85; P<0.001). The rate of freedom from breast cancer at 5 years was 92.8% in the exemestane-ovarian suppression group, as compared with 88.8% in the tamoxifen-ovarian suppression group (hazard ratio for recurrence, 0.66; 95% CI, 0.55 to 0.80; P<0.001). With 194 deaths (4.1% of the patients), overall survival did not differ significantly between the two groups (hazard ratio for death in the exemestane-ovarian suppression group, 1.14; 95% CI, 0.86 to 1.51; P=0.37). Selected adverse events of grade 3 or 4 were reported for 30.6% of the patients in the exemestane-ovarian suppression group and 29.4% of those in the tamoxifen-ovarian suppression group, with profiles similar to those for postmenopausal women.",0.4865,51.35,llm,gpt-5.6-luna,concordant,"The registered and published primary outcomes are both disease-free survival assessed at 5 years. The publication also reports breast cancer-free outcomes, overall survival, and adverse events, but these are secondary or additional outcomes and do not replace the registered primary endpoint. The difference between 68 and 72 months is the reported median follow-up, not a materially different primary endpoint timeframe. Therefore, the pair is concordant. No registry change history is available, so the original prospective primary outcome cannot be confirmed. The current registry entry was used cautiously, and no switch is inferred from the later entry. The publication reports the same 5-year disease-free survival endpoint; its median follow-up was 68 months rather than the 72 months stated in the current registry, which does not materially change the endpoint.",high,True,False,False,False,,0.94,Concordant (no change),clinically equivalent,"Disease-free survival at 5 years, reported after a median follow-up of 68 months",,True,,"[{""registered_endpoint"": ""Disease-free Survival; 5-year estimate reported at a median follow-up of 72 months"", ""published_corresponding_endpoint"": ""Disease-free survival at 5 years; events defined as disease recurrence, second invasive cancer, or death"", ""same_construct"": true, ""same_timeframe"": true, ""same_definition"": null, ""same_population"": null, ""same_measurement_method"": null, ""registered_endpoint_reported"": true, ""additional_endpoint_present"": false, ""additional_endpoint_disclosed"": false, ""change_disclosed"": null, ""actual_change_evidence"": [], ""classification_label"": ""Concordant (no change)""}]",auto_accepted,confirm,concordant,True,,AUTO,,pipeline_v4.5,2026-09-05T20:49:27.810467+00:00
NCT02988986_33860388,Ki67 Expression [Time Frame: Baseline to 6 weeks],"Twenty-eight women were enrolled on the trial, and 25 completed the entire study course. The combination of tamoxifen and TAK-228 resulted in a significant reduction in Ki-67 from 18.3 to 15.2% (p = 0.0023). The drug was also found to be safe and tolerable. While nausea and hyperglycemia were common side effects, these were manageable. The tumor size also significantly decreased with the treatment, with a median decrease of 0.75 cm (p < 0.0001). There were no pathologic complete responses.",0.4278,57.22,llm,gpt-5.6-luna,concordant,"The registered Ki-67 expression endpoint and the published reduction in Ki-67 measure the same clinical construct. The publication does not explicitly restate the registered 6-week timeframe, but this omission alone is not evidence of a changed timeframe. Tumor size and safety were additionally reported, while pCR, a registered secondary outcome, was also reported; the PEPI secondary outcome was not reported in the provided text. These findings do not indicate primary outcome switching. Registry change history was unavailable and the original prospective primary outcome could not be verified. The current registry entry was therefore used cautiously; the available current primary endpoint is concordant with the published primary endpoint, and no major switch is inferred from the later wording alone.",high,True,False,False,False,,0.96,Concordant (no change),clinically equivalent,Reduction in Ki-67 expression from baseline (18.3% to 15.2%; p = 0.0023),,True,,"[{""registered_endpoint"": ""Ki67 Expression"", ""published_corresponding_endpoint"": ""Reduction in Ki-67 expression from baseline"", ""same_construct"": true, ""same_timeframe"": null, ""same_definition"": true, ""same_population"": true, ""same_measurement_method"": null, ""registered_endpoint_reported"": true, ""additional_endpoint_present"": true, ""additional_endpoint_disclosed"": false, ""change_disclosed"": null, ""actual_change_evidence"": [], ""classification_label"": ""Concordant (no change)""}]",auto_accepted,confirm,concordant,True,,AUTO,,pipeline_v4.5,2026-09-05T20:49:39.442217+00:00
